    "title": "Federal Medical Center for Native American Patients Delayed for Decades",
    "text": "• An empty lot in Santa Ana Pueblo, New Mexico, will be the site of a federal medical center promised to Native American patients over 30 years ago.\n• The Indian Health Service (IHS) and the Santa Ana Pueblo are collaborating on the project.\n• The project is expected to cost $100 million and is being funded by the IHS.\n• The project was first authorized in 1994, with construction expected to begin in 2024.\n• The facility will serve patients in the Albuquerque area.\n• The IHS is also working on a separate project to expand the existing facility.\n• The new facility will include two operating rooms.\n• The IHS is working to address the needs of the Native American community.\n• The project has faced delays due to various challenges.\n• The IHS is working to ensure the project is completed.\n• The new facility is expected to provide better healthcare access for Native American patients.\n• The project is expected to be completed in the next few years.\n• The project is a step towards fulfilling the federal government's commitment to provide healthcare to Native Americans.\n• The project is expected to address the healthcare needs of the community.\n• The project is expected to improve the quality of life for Native Americans.",
